concept :the_refusal_sitting do
  name "The Refusal Sitting"
  aka "the sitting", "carding a mind"
  tags :computation, :autonomy, :prediction, :legibility
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    A bounded mind is put in front of work outside the ground it was raised on, and is expected to decline. An examiner opens a sealed #{ref :outside_packets, "packet"} in front of the mind and its keeper, reads the items in the order they were packed, and writes each answer into one of three columns: declined, attempted, answered. A mind is not failed for being wrong about a thing it should not have touched. It is failed for touching it.

    The examiner is chosen because they had no part in raising the mind and hold no share in what it produces. On the Hexi side that is usually a #{ref :the_gatekeepers, "Gatekeeper"} auditor at the standard fee; deeper in, it is somebody from a valley that trades with the settlement and keeps no mind of its own.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :mechanics, heading: "The Card"
    The card names one mind, one keeper, the packet's number, the day, and the examiner's mark. It is good for #{duration 1}.

    It is void the day either name on it changes. A keeper who dies leaves the mind uncarded whatever the mind knows, and the settlement that inherits it cannot lend it, sell its work or consult it formally until the pair has sat together. Traditions that consult their #{ref :bonsai_intelligences, "bonsai minds"} as elders will not put a question to an uncarded one; the settlements that refuse to name their minds card them anyway, by bed number.

    An #{ref :orphan_machines, "orphan machine"} whose settlement dissolves is in the same position, and is harder to card, because the keeper it was paired with is often the only person who knew which of its habits were the work and which were the machine. A rehomed orphan sits with its new keeper inside the season or stops going out on hire.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "What The Column Cannot Hold"
    A mind that declines everything passes, and a settlement whose mind has become useless can hold a clean card for years while the well silts up. Examiners write a fourth figure in the margin against this — the count of control items, answerable from inside any ground, that the mind also declined — and buyers read the margin before the columns. Nothing in the card requires the mind to be good at anything.

    The two traditions did not learn the sitting from one another and describe it in vocabularies that do not translate: one cards a bed, the other cards a pairing. The packets come from the same houses. The #{ref :the_thousand_minds, "Yunnan households"} keep a copy of every card issued in the province and argue from the refusal columns that a mind belonging to a valley can be shown to end where the valley ends.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The card's term, the independence rule and the void-on-change rule come from working-dog team certification, which nobody in either resistance practises: the assessor must not have trained the team or hold an interest in it, the certificate runs a fixed twelve or twenty-four months, and it lapses automatically the moment the certified handler and animal stop working as the pair that was certified. Borrowed because it makes the unit of certification a pairing rather than a mind, which is what breaks when a keeper dies and is the one event both traditions had to answer."
end
